1. Per-node, transport-only knob. It is read once (OnceLock) and clamped to the 8 MB floor (bridge.rs:118-154). It is used only by the pre-proposal push (bridge.rs:431-446). Receivers handle both 0xFD and 0xFC (swarm.rs:1661-1704).
2. Bodies are content-addressed. compute_action_hash covers the canonical bytes, the nonce and the domain-tagged signature (torus-types lib.rs:1183-1216). Absorbed pulls are stored under a recomputed hash (native_da.rs:97-123; app.rs:6475-6491).
3. The proposer flushes its ingress mirror before selection, then writes any still-absent body durably before sending the bundle (app.rs:7130-7198). A manifest therefore never names a body the proposer cannot serve.
4. A missing body cannot cause a wrong vote. The vote waits on check_proposal_data, which absorbs pulled bodies and checks DA presence, re-checking every 20 ms (implementation.rs:2646-2709, 3592; app.rs:7022-7090). A MissingData body is parked and retried every 500 ms, with a 3 s fallback to sync (implementation.rs:3252-3334). The hot path hands misses to the off-thread recovery worker (app.rs:6449-6465).
