candidates.mechanism:
The consensus gossip limiter allows 50 messages per second per author (config.rs:280, enforced at swarm.rs:1494). In fast idle stretches it drops a leader's ProposalHeader, and the view then times out after 1.2 s. The s75 fix-D re-send already exists: tick_header_resend_at re-sends the same header directly to every other validator while the leader is still in its own view one interval after proposing. Its default interval is 3,000 ms, so it never fires before the 1,200 ms timeout. On the 10m depth-1 cell p4tail10-10m-r1-a1 the logs contain 0 'header re-send' lines.

The direct path (send -> /torus/direct -> swarm.rs:1725 handle_consensus_direct_traced -> enqueue) never touches ConsensusRateLimiter. So a 250 ms interval turns each header-drop stall into a gap of about 0.25-0.3 s.

Why this differs from TORUS_CONSENSUS_DIRECT_FAN=1: the per-author bucket stays in place and still paces idle views at about 22/s, the same as today's bursty average (idle_blk_s 16-19). So there is no flood of empty blocks into exec or into the depth-1 bench tail.

The receiver side is already safe:
- a repeated header keeps the body fetch already running (implementation.rs:2420-2424);
- each node votes at most once per view (highest_view_voted);
- the same block hash is not equivocation;
- a follower that is one view behind takes the existing round-skip path.

